WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.873 --> 00:00:16.994
scrimmage against the Swallows was an away game.

2
00:00:17.854 --> 00:00:20.295
"I'm ready," Patrick repeated under his breath.

3
00:00:20.856 --> 00:00:22.796
But he hadn't gotten much sleep the night before.

4
00:00:23.777 --> 00:00:28.399
His math quiz with a red 57 had sat on his desk like a warning light.

5
00:00:29.139 --> 00:00:31.600
And he'd been worried about who would start as catcher today.

6
00:00:33.348 --> 00:00:37.890
Patrick rubbed his lucky catcher's mitt as Coach slapped the roster on the dugout wall.

7
00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:40.031
"Here's the lineup, boys.

8
00:00:40.531 --> 00:00:41.611
Ready to play baseball?"

9
00:00:41.631 --> 00:00:43.852
"Yeah!" roared the team.

10
00:00:44.773 --> 00:00:47.954
Patrick took a deep breath and went over to look at the roster.

11
00:00:51.095 --> 00:00:54.097
Second up for bat, Patrick Deboe, Number 12.

12
00:00:55.017 --> 00:00:56.137
Dell flashed him a grin.

13
00:00:56.157 --> 00:00:57.518
"Mickey's good.

14
00:00:57.938 --> 00:01:00.079
But you and I have got the dance down."

15
00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:02.320
Patrick grinned too.

16
00:01:03.136 --> 00:01:08.618
He and Dell were good dance partners, meaning that as pitcher and catcher, they could follow each other's

17
00:01:08.678 --> 00:01:09.699
moves instinctively.

18
00:01:09.719 --> 00:01:11.620
"Play ball!"

19
00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:15.021
the umpire yelled a few minutes later.

20
00:01:16.081 --> 00:01:17.342
The Dragons were up first.

21
00:01:18.022 --> 00:01:19.543
Patrick managed to hit a single.

22
00:01:22.644 --> 00:01:26.025
But the next three batters struck out, so the Dragons went scoreless.

23
00:01:28.947 --> 00:01:32.388
Dell headed to the mound while Patrick took his position behind home plate.

24
00:01:34.732 --> 00:01:35.332
"First game.

25
00:01:35.452 --> 00:01:37.133
First pitch," he thought happily.

26
00:01:37.793 --> 00:01:42.015
Mickey was a nice guy, but beating him for the starter position sure felt sweet.

27
00:01:42.955 --> 00:01:45.596
Now he had to prove he deserved to keep the position.

28
00:01:46.477 --> 00:01:49.118
The first batter up for the other team was Number 14.

29
00:01:49.898 --> 00:01:52.879
Patrick remembered that this batter was the one who crowded the plate.

30
00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:56.941
Patrick put down one finger to signal a fast pitch.

31
00:01:57.641 --> 00:01:59.462
Dell wound up and whizzed it in.

32
00:02:02.023 --> 00:02:03.784
"Strike!" called the umpire.

33
00:02:04.716 --> 00:02:05.957
Patrick nodded at Dell.

34
00:02:06.577 --> 00:02:10.339
Two more pitches, two more strikes, and they had their first out.

35
00:02:10.359 --> 00:02:12.260
"Nice work, you two!"

36
00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:13.361
called Daniel.

37
00:02:13.381 --> 00:02:16.022
"Finally, a compliment from Daniel!"

38
00:02:16.362 --> 00:02:17.023
Patrick thought.

39
00:02:18.003 --> 00:02:21.725
Number 42 tapped his cleats with the bat and planted his feet in the dirt.

40
00:02:24.527 --> 00:02:26.768
Patrick remembered that this kid was a good hitter.

41
00:02:27.308 --> 00:02:30.470
He put down two fingers to signal a curve ball to Dell.

42
00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:34.312
Swoosh. "Strike!"

43
00:02:35.104 --> 00:02:38.285
The batter caught a piece of the next pitch, but the ball went foul.

44
00:02:39.606 --> 00:02:40.967
Patrick caught it easily.

45
00:02:41.927 --> 00:02:42.707
Patrick grinned.

46
00:02:43.267 --> 00:02:44.588
They had two outs already.

47
00:02:46.169 --> 00:02:49.070
In middle school baseball, the teams played seven innings.

48
00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:53.572
By the bottom of the final inning, the Dragons were ahead, 7-6.

49
00:02:54.572 --> 00:02:56.813
Number 42 for the Swallows was up again.

50
00:02:57.573 --> 00:03:00.635
"He looks ready to slam a homerun," thought Patrick.

51
00:03:01.775 --> 00:03:03.436
He signaled Dell for the changeup.

52
00:03:03.916 --> 00:03:07.697
Dell's pitch was high, but Number 42 hit it solidly.

53
00:03:09.418 --> 00:03:12.058
The ball sailed just inside third base.

54
00:03:12.818 --> 00:03:14.699
In left field Todd dove for it.

55
00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:20.480
Patrick held his breath as Todd rolled on the field.

56
00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:23.681
Would Todd come up with it?

57
00:03:23.701 --> 00:03:29.403
"Yes!" screamed Patrick, seeing Todd's glove firmly wrapped around the ball.

58
00:03:30.423 --> 00:03:31.063
Two outs!

59
00:03:31.623 --> 00:03:33.524
One more out and the Dragons would win!

60
00:03:34.528 --> 00:03:39.029
Then everyone got quiet—Todd was still lying on the field.

61
00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:41.950
"Oh no," Patrick thought.

62
00:03:43.491 --> 00:03:45.551
Coach jogged out to check Todd's injury.

63
00:03:48.072 --> 00:03:52.133
Minutes later Todd stood, gingerly holding his arm against his chest.

64
00:03:57.475 --> 00:04:01.236
The crowd clapped as he walked off the field with Coach and over to his parents.

65
00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:04.882
Coach hurried over to the dugout and motioned for Mickey.

66
00:04:05.522 --> 00:04:06.663
Then he looked at Patrick.

67
00:04:06.683 --> 00:04:08.764
"Take left field, Patrick.

68
00:04:09.245 --> 00:04:12.547
This next batter hits deep, so we need someone with experience.

69
00:04:13.127 --> 00:04:14.368
Mickey will go in as catcher."

70
00:04:14.388 --> 00:04:17.470
"Okay, Coach," Patrick mumbled.

71
00:04:18.311 --> 00:04:20.672
He pulled off his catcher equipment and found his glove.

72
00:04:22.614 --> 00:04:25.696
As he put on his cap, he glanced at the Swallows' next batter.

73
00:04:26.536 --> 00:04:28.077
This kid liked the pitches low.

74
00:04:28.457 --> 00:04:29.518
Should he warn Mickey?

75
00:04:29.538 --> 00:04:33.029
"Nah. That's Daniel's job," thought Patrick.

76
00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:35.971
Dell's first pitch was a strike.

77
00:04:36.612 --> 00:04:39.914
Then a wild pitch from Dell put the Swallows batter on base.

78
00:04:39.934 --> 00:04:43.177
"That wasn't Mickey's fault," Patrick thought.

79
00:04:43.757 --> 00:04:45.779
But still the catcher always took the blame.

80
00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:47.741
It was just part of the job.

81
00:04:48.741 --> 00:04:52.144
The next batter had a chance to bring in the runner and tie up the score.

82
00:04:53.085 --> 00:04:55.587
Dell sent the pitch in, low and outside.

83
00:04:56.988 --> 00:04:57.909
The batter swung.

84
00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:01.392
The ball popped up behind home plate.

85
00:05:02.024 --> 00:05:04.466
Mickey scrambled to catch it, pulling off his mask.

86
00:05:07.308 --> 00:05:15.195
The ball drifted near the fence and then fell down, down Mickey stretched over the fence, teetering to

87
00:05:15.255 --> 00:05:16.015
keep his balance.

88
00:05:16.656 --> 00:05:19.038
The ball settled solidly into his mitt.

89
00:05:20.499 --> 00:05:22.000
"Out!" cried the umpire.

90
00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:23.281
"Game over!"

91
00:05:26.324 --> 00:05:27.585
The Dragons had won!

92
00:05:28.305 --> 00:05:31.288
The team swarmed around home plate to congratulate Mickey.

93
00:05:32.492 --> 00:05:33.872
"What an amazing catch!"

94
00:05:34.393 --> 00:05:35.973
Patrick clapped Mickey on the back.

95
00:05:35.993 --> 00:05:38.554
"Thanks." Mickey grinned.

96
00:05:38.574 --> 00:05:41.915
"Another inch outside the fence and I wouldn't have reached it."

97
00:05:42.615 --> 00:05:45.456
The two of them joined the line to shake hands with the other team.

98
00:05:48.797 --> 00:05:53.218
Patrick tapped the hand of the Swallows player who had made the last out, feeling sorry for the

99
00:05:53.258 --> 00:05:57.039
guy. It was bad luck to be the hitter who made the last out.

100
00:05:57.659 --> 00:06:00.660
In the dugout everyone kept raving about Mickey's catch.

101
00:06:01.752 --> 00:06:06.015
Patrick was glad his team had won, but he felt a little jealous that he had missed the

102
00:06:06.035 --> 00:06:06.635
main action.

103
00:06:06.655 --> 00:06:09.717
"It's just one game," he told himself.

104
00:06:09.737 --> 00:06:13.939
"Next time you'll be back where you belong—behind home plate."

105
00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:17.802
"Huh?" Patrick said the next morning at school.

106
00:06:18.582 --> 00:06:20.023
Dell repeated the bad news.

107
00:06:20.764 --> 00:06:22.044
"Todd injured his shoulder.

108
00:06:22.745 --> 00:06:24.086
He's out for at least a week."

109
00:06:25.046 --> 00:06:26.747
"He can't play against the Bandits?"

110
00:06:27.267 --> 00:06:27.888
asked Patrick.

111
00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:34.212
Patrick had already started memorizing the Bandits' roster, the first team on the Dragons' regular schedule.

112
00:06:34.232 --> 00:06:36.594
"Nope." Dell looked grim.

113
00:06:36.614 --> 00:06:40.237
"And it will be a challenge to beat them without our star hitter."

114
00:06:40.257 --> 00:06:43.039
"You're right," Patrick agreed.

115
00:06:43.059 --> 00:06:46.923
"And His heart sank at another realization.

116
00:06:46.943 --> 00:06:48.844
"Mickey is a good hitter.

117
00:06:49.425 --> 00:06:51.246
Coach will probably start him as catcher."

118
00:06:51.266 --> 00:06:56.250
"Yep. In three weeks we play the Hornets—our biggest rivals.

119
00:06:56.971 --> 00:06:58.292
I hope Todd's back by then."

120
00:06:59.148 --> 00:06:59.889
Patrick nodded.

121
00:07:00.409 --> 00:07:02.270
He hoped Todd would be back by then too.

122
00:07:04.131 --> 00:07:06.973
The weather for practice after school was cold and dreary.

123
00:07:07.954 --> 00:07:11.777
Patrick worked with the fielders while Daniel spent extra time coaching Mickey.

124
00:07:12.717 --> 00:07:15.499
Patrick couldn't help glancing toward home plate a few times.

125
00:07:15.519 --> 00:07:17.581
"Way to go, Mickey!"

126
00:07:17.901 --> 00:07:18.741
Daniel kept saying.

127
00:07:18.761 --> 00:07:20.983
"You're framing pitches really well."

128
00:07:21.783 --> 00:07:25.426
Just then a ball thrown by the center fielder sailed past Patrick.

129
00:07:26.707 --> 00:07:28.268
"Patrick!" snapped Coach.

130
00:07:29.016 --> 00:07:30.797
"Are you picking dandelions out there?

131
00:07:31.058 --> 00:07:31.858
Where's your head?"

132
00:07:31.878 --> 00:07:34.780
"Sorry," muttered Patrick.

133
00:07:35.381 --> 00:07:36.701
He ran to retrieve the ball.

134
00:07:39.183 --> 00:07:40.064
"Pay attention!"

135
00:07:40.404 --> 00:07:41.345
he scolded himself.

136
00:07:42.165 --> 00:07:47.089
If he wasn't careful, he'd be sitting on the bench during games, with most of the other seventh-graders.

137
00:07:49.871 --> 00:07:52.613
Finally rain forced Coach to shorten practice.

138
00:07:53.153 --> 00:07:55.555
For once Patrick didn't mind going home early.

139
00:07:56.415 --> 00:07:57.296
He needed to study.

140
00:07:57.876 --> 00:08:02.899
His grade on the last math quiz had been better—but it wasn't good enough to satisfy his mother.
